{"p13-l01":[{"id":"p13-l01-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Closed-loop DC gain with a loop gain of 20?</p>\n","explain":"<p>L/(1 + L).</p>\n","answer":0.9524,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l01-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Sensitivity S at DC with a loop gain of 20?</p>\n","explain":"<p>1/(1 + L).</p>\n","answer":0.0476,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l01-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Output error in % with the prefilter when the plant gain is 30 % high (L goes from 20 to 26)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>About 27 times less than open loop.</p>\n","answer":1.11,"tol":0.01,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p13-l01-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Closed-loop time constant in ms for τ = 0.5 s and L = 20?</p>\n","explain":"<p>τ/(1 + L).</p>\n","answer":23.8,"tol":0.01,"unit":"ms"},{"id":"p13-l01-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>What can feedback not correct?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The loop tracks the measured value.</p>\n","options":["changes in plant gain","errors in the sensor","slow plant dynamics","load disturbances"],"answer":1},{"id":"p13-l01-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>What is the main risk of raising loop gain?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Dynamics and delays make high gain oscillate.</p>\n","options":["slower response","higher sensitivity to plant changes","lower accuracy","instability"],"answer":3}],"p13-l02":[{"id":"p13-l02-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Motor damping β in N·m·s for R = 1.2 Ω, k = 0.05, b = 2e-5?</p>\n","explain":"<p>k²/R + b.</p>\n","answer":0.002103,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l02-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Open-loop speed drop in rad/s for a 0.05 N·m load?</p>\n","explain":"<p>τ_L/β.</p>\n","answer":23.77,"tol":0.003,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l02-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Loop gain with K_p = 0.5 V per rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>kK_p/(Rβ).</p>\n","answer":9.906,"tol":0.003,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l02-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Closed-loop speed drop in rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Open-loop drop over 1 + L.</p>\n","answer":2.181,"tol":0.005,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l02-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>The disturbance transfer function with feedback is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The same sensitivity factor.</p>\n","options":["G_d/(1 + GK)","GK/(1 + GK)","1 + GK","G_d·GK"],"answer":0},{"id":"p13-l02-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Proportional speed feedback against a step load leaves…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Integral action is needed for zero error.</p>\n","options":["an oscillation","zero steady error","a smaller but non-zero steady speed error","a larger error"],"answer":2}],"p13-l03":[{"id":"p13-l03-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Largest stable K for K/((s + 1)(s + 2)(s + 3))?</p>\n","explain":"<p>a₂a₁ = a₃a₀ at the limit.</p>\n","answer":60,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l03-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Oscillation frequency in rad/s at that gain?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Auxiliary polynomial 6s² + 66.</p>\n","answer":3.317,"tol":0.001,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l03-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Number of RHP roots of s⁴ + s³ + 2s² + 2s + 3?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The epsilon method shows two sign changes.</p>\n","answer":2,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l03-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Upper gain limit for s³ + 2s² + (K + 1)s + 3K?</p>\n","explain":"<p>From the s¹ row.</p>\n","answer":2,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l03-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>A row of zeros in the Routh array means…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Use the auxiliary polynomial.</p>\n","options":["roots symmetric about the origin, such as a pair on the imaginary axis","an arithmetic mistake","a root at infinity","the system is always stable"],"answer":0},{"id":"p13-l03-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>All coefficients positive guarantees stability for…</p>\n","explain":"<p>From third order on you need the full test.</p>\n","options":["first- and second-order polynomials only","no polynomial","odd orders only","every polynomial"],"answer":0}],"p13-l04":[{"id":"p13-l04-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Step error of the type 0 example?</p>\n","explain":"<p>1/(1 + K_p) with K_p = 5.</p>\n","answer":0.1667,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l04-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Ramp error of the type 1 example?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_v = 10/(2·5).</p>\n","answer":1,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l04-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Parabola error of the type 2 example?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_a = 10·1/5 = 2.</p>\n","answer":0.5,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l04-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Following error in rad for a 2 rad/s ramp with K_v = 50 s⁻¹?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Ramp rate over K_v.</p>\n","answer":0.04,"tol":0.001,"unit":"rad"},{"id":"p13-l04-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>A type 1 loop tracking a step has…</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p is infinite.</p>\n","options":["error 1/(1 + K_p)","error 1/K_v","an error that grows","zero steady-state error"],"answer":3},{"id":"p13-l04-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The final value theorem applies only if…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Otherwise there is no final value.</p>\n","options":["the input is a step","the closed loop is stable","the system is type 0","the plant has no zeros"],"answer":1}],"p13-l05":[{"id":"p13-l05-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Steady error for a type 0 loop with K_p = 9?</p>\n","explain":"<p>1/(1 + K_p).</p>\n","answer":0.1,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l05-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>DC gain of the motor in (rad/s)/V?</p>\n","explain":"<p>k/(Rb + k²).</p>\n","answer":19.81,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l05-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Gain K_p where the two poles meet?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Discriminant zero.</p>\n","answer":13.27,"tol":0.005,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l05-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Overshoot in % at ζ = 0.707?</p>\n","explain":"<p>exp(−πζ/√(1−ζ²)).</p>\n","answer":4.32,"tol":0.01,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p13-l05-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Raising proportional gain on this loop…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Only the constant term changes.</p>\n","options":["slows the response","moves the pole sum","removes the steady error completely","shrinks the error and reduces damping"],"answer":3},{"id":"p13-l05-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The pole sum stays fixed because…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Sum of roots = −a₁/a₀.</p>\n","options":["the motor is linear","the inductance is small","the gain only changes the constant coefficient","the poles are real"],"answer":2}],"p13-l06":[{"id":"p13-l06-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Zero location in rad/s of a PI with K_p = 0.12 and K_i = 2.5 (give the magnitude)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_i/K_p.</p>\n","answer":20.83,"tol":0.002,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l06-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Steady error in % of P-only control with loop DC gain 2.38?</p>\n","explain":"<p>1/(1 + K).</p>\n","answer":29.6,"tol":0.01,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p13-l06-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>P-only load droop in rad/s for 0.05 N·m (β + kK_p/R = 0.007103)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>τ_L over the total damping.</p>\n","answer":7.04,"tol":0.01,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l06-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Steady error with PI against a constant load?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Type 1 rejects constants.</p>\n","answer":0,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l06-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>The PI controller adds…</p>\n","explain":"<p>C(s) = (K_p s + K_i)/s.</p>\n","options":["a pole at −K_i/K_p","two zeros","only gain","a pole at the origin and a zero at −K_i/K_p"],"answer":3},{"id":"p13-l06-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The price of integral action is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Up to 90° lag below the zero.</p>\n","options":["slower rejection of noise only","steady error","lower DC gain","phase lag that reduces stability margins"],"answer":3}],"p13-l07":[{"id":"p13-l07-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Minimum proportional gain in N/rad for the linear cart-pole to have stiffness (p² = 19.9, β = 1.93)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p &gt; p²/β.</p>\n","answer":10.31,"tol":0.005,"unit":"N/rad"},{"id":"p13-l07-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Natural frequency in rad/s with K_p = 38?</p>\n","explain":"<p>√(βK_p − p²).</p>\n","answer":7.32,"tol":0.005,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l07-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Damping ratio with K_d = 7?</p>\n","explain":"<p>βK_d/(2ω_n).</p>\n","answer":0.924,"tol":0.005,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l07-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>K_d for ζ = 0.7 at K_p = 38?</p>\n","explain":"<p>2ζω_n/β.</p>\n","answer":5.3,"tol":0.01,"unit":"N·s/rad"},{"id":"p13-l07-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Which term provides damping on the inverted pendulum?</p>\n","explain":"<p>It opposes angular velocity.</p>\n","options":["derivative","proportional","integral","none of them"],"answer":0},{"id":"p13-l07-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why are the lab’s cart-position gains positive?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Non-minimum-phase behaviour.</p>\n","options":["you must lean the pole towards where the cart should go, by first moving the cart away","it’s a sign error","the rail is tilted","to make the cart drift"],"answer":0}],"p13-l08":[{"id":"p13-l08-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>RMS in rad/s of a raw derivative of 0.0087 rad white noise sampled at 5 ms?</p>\n","explain":"<p>√2 σ/T_s.</p>\n","answer":2.46,"tol":0.01,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l08-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Filter coefficient a for T_f = 12 ms and T_s = 5 ms?</p>\n","explain":"<p>e^(−T_s/T_f).</p>\n","answer":0.659,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l08-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Factor by which that filter reduces derivative noise RMS?</p>\n","explain":"<p>√2 over (1 − a)√(2/(1 + a)).</p>\n","answer":3.78,"tol":0.01,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l08-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase lag in degrees of a 100 ms filter at 7 rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>arctan(ωT_f).</p>\n","answer":35,"tol":0.01,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l08-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>High-frequency gain of K_d s/(T_f s + 1)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The filter caps it.</p>\n","options":["zero","K_d","infinite","K_d/T_f"],"answer":3},{"id":"p13-l08-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>What limits how much you can filter the derivative?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Damping that arrives late is no damping.</p>\n","options":["the integral winds up","the phase lag erodes the damping","nothing","the actuator saturates more"],"answer":1}],"p13-l09":[{"id":"p13-l09-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Voltage in V the PI asks for at the first instant of a 200 rad/s step with K_p = 0.12?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p e, before any integral.</p>\n","answer":24,"tol":0.001,"unit":"V"},{"id":"p13-l09-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Integral time T_i in ms for K_p = 0.12 and K_i = 2.5?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p/K_i.</p>\n","answer":48,"tol":0.001,"unit":"ms"},{"id":"p13-l09-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Steady voltage in V needed for 200 rad/s with a DC gain of 19.81 (rad/s)/V?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Within the 12 V limit.</p>\n","answer":10.1,"tol":0.003,"unit":"V"},{"id":"p13-l09-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Largest step in rad/s that doesn’t saturate a 12 V drive at the first instant with K_p = 0.12?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p e ≤ V_max.</p>\n","answer":100,"tol":0.001,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l09-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Back-calculation drives the integrator using…</p>\n","explain":"<p>(u − v)/T_t.</p>\n","options":["the motor current","the difference between the saturated and unsaturated output","a separate model","the derivative of the error"],"answer":1},{"id":"p13-l09-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Without anti-windup, saturation typically causes…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The stored integral has to unwind.</p>\n","options":["zero overshoot","faster settling","a steady error","larger overshoot and slower settling"],"answer":3}],"p13-l10":[{"id":"p13-l10-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Ultimate gain of 1/(s + 1)³?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The gain magnitude at √3 rad/s is 1/8.</p>\n","answer":8,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l10-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Ultimate period in s of 1/(s + 1)³?</p>\n","explain":"<p>2π/√3.</p>\n","answer":3.628,"tol":0.002,"unit":"s"},{"id":"p13-l10-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Describing-function gain of a ±1 relay when the output oscillates ±0.16?</p>\n","explain":"<p>4d/(πa).</p>\n","answer":7.96,"tol":0.005,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l10-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Ziegler-Nichols K_p for K_u = 8?</p>\n","explain":"<p>0.6 K_u.</p>\n","answer":4.8,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l10-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why use a relay rather than raising P gain to find K_u?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The experiment stays small and safe.</p>\n","options":["it’s more accurate than the exact value","the oscillation amplitude is controlled by the relay level","it gives zero steady error","it doesn’t need a plant"],"answer":1},{"id":"p13-l10-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Ziegler-Nichols PID tunings are typically…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Detune them in practice.</p>\n","options":["very conservative","unstable","aggressive, with large overshoot","optimal for noise"],"answer":2}],"p13-l11":[{"id":"p13-l11-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Asymptote centroid of 1/(s(s + 2)(s + 4))?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Sum of poles over n − m.</p>\n","answer":-2,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l11-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Breakaway point of that locus?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Root of 3s² + 12s + 8 between the poles.</p>\n","answer":-0.8453,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l11-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Gain at the breakaway point?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K = |s||s + 2||s + 4|.</p>\n","answer":3.079,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l11-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Gain at which it crosses into the right half-plane?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Routh.</p>\n","answer":48,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l11-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>A point is on the root locus when…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The magnitude then gives K.</p>\n","options":["it is a pole of L","L(s) is real","the angle of L(s) is 180° (mod 360°)","|L(s)| = 1"],"answer":2},{"id":"p13-l11-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>As K → ∞, branches end at…</p>\n","explain":"<p>D + KN ≈ KN.</p>\n","options":["the imaginary axis","the open-loop zeros, or infinity along asymptotes","the origin","the open-loop poles"],"answer":1}],"p13-l12":[{"id":"p13-l12-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>α for a lead that adds 42° at most?</p>\n","explain":"<p>(1 − sin φ)/(1 + sin φ).</p>\n","answer":0.198,"tol":0.005,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l12-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Maximum phase in degrees of a lead with α = 0.1?</p>\n","explain":"<p>arcsin((1 − α)/(1 + α)).</p>\n","answer":54.9,"tol":0.005,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l12-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Lead gain in dB at ω_m for α = 0.198?</p>\n","explain":"<p>1/√α.</p>\n","answer":7.03,"tol":0.01,"unit":"dB"},{"id":"p13-l12-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase margin in degrees of 10/(s(s + 1)) without compensation?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Crossover at 3.08 rad/s.</p>\n","answer":17.96,"tol":0.005,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l12-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>A lag compensator mainly…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Its corner sits a decade below crossover.</p>\n","options":["speeds up the response","raises low-frequency gain without moving crossover much","adds phase at crossover","removes the integrator"],"answer":1},{"id":"p13-l12-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Where should a lead’s maximum phase be placed?</p>\n","explain":"<p>That is where phase margin is measured.</p>\n","options":["at the new gain crossover frequency","far above crossover","at the plant pole","at DC"],"answer":0}],"p13-l13":[{"id":"p13-l13-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Error in dB of a real-pole asymptote at its corner?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The exact gain there is 1/√2.</p>\n","answer":3.01,"tol":0.002,"unit":"dB"},{"id":"p13-l13-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Resonant peak above the asymptote in dB for ζ = 0.1?</p>\n","explain":"<p>−20 log₁₀(2ζ).</p>\n","answer":13.98,"tol":0.002,"unit":"dB"},{"id":"p13-l13-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Exact gain in dB of the worked example at 10 rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The corner’s 3 dB; the other factors nearly cancel.</p>\n","answer":-3.01,"tol":0.01,"unit":"dB"},{"id":"p13-l13-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>High-frequency slope in dB/decade of the worked example?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Three poles, one zero.</p>\n","answer":-40,"tol":0,"unit":"dB/dec"},{"id":"p13-l13-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why do Bode plots add factor by factor?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Phase adds directly too.</p>\n","options":["the poles are real","scipy does it that way","frequencies add","the logarithm of a product is a sum of logarithms"],"answer":3},{"id":"p13-l13-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>A complex pair’s phase at its natural frequency is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Half of its total −180°.</p>\n","options":["−180°","0°","−45°","−90°"],"answer":3}],"p13-l14":[{"id":"p13-l14-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Closed-loop RHP poles if P = 1 and the plot encircles −1 once clockwise?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Z = N + P.</p>\n","answer":2,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l14-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Encirclements needed for stability when P = 2 (counting clockwise as positive)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Two counter-clockwise.</p>\n","answer":-2,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l14-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Where does L = K/((s − 1)(s + 2)) cross the negative real axis at ω = 0 for K = 3?</p>\n","explain":"<p>L(0) = −K/2.</p>\n","answer":-1.5,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l14-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Smallest K that stabilises K/((s − 1)(s + 2))?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The constant term K − 2 must be positive.</p>\n","answer":2,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l14-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>The zeros of 1 + L(s) are…</p>\n","explain":"<p>1 + L = (D + N)/D.</p>\n","options":["the open-loop zeros","the closed-loop poles","the open-loop poles","always stable"],"answer":1},{"id":"p13-l14-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why indent the contour around poles on the imaginary axis?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The detour maps to a large arc.</p>\n","options":["L is infinite there, so the contour must avoid them","to count zeros","to remove the integrator","to make the plot symmetric"],"answer":0}],"p13-l15":[{"id":"p13-l15-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Gain margin of 2/(s(s + 1)(s + 2))?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Routh limit 6 over the current gain 2.</p>\n","answer":3,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l15-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>That gain margin in dB?</p>\n","explain":"<p>20 log₁₀ 3.</p>\n","answer":9.54,"tol":0.002,"unit":"dB"},{"id":"p13-l15-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Delay margin in s with PM = 32.6° at 0.749 rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>PM in radians over ω_c.</p>\n","answer":0.76,"tol":0.005,"unit":"s"},{"id":"p13-l15-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase in degrees lost to a 3.5 ms delay at 20 rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>ωτ.</p>\n","answer":4.01,"tol":0.01,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l15-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>A pure time delay changes…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Its magnitude is 1 at all frequencies.</p>\n","options":["gain only","phase only, by −ωτ","both gain and phase","nothing"],"answer":1},{"id":"p13-l15-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>At the gain limit the loop oscillates at…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Where the phase is −180°.</p>\n","options":["the phase crossover frequency","the highest plant pole","DC","the gain crossover frequency"],"answer":0}],"p13-l16":[{"id":"p13-l16-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>S + T at any frequency?</p>\n","explain":"<p>(1 + L)/(1 + L).</p>\n","answer":1,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l16-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Guaranteed gain margin for M_s = 2?</p>\n","explain":"<p>M_s/(M_s − 1).</p>\n","answer":2,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l16-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Guaranteed phase margin in degrees for M_s = 2?</p>\n","explain":"<p>2 arcsin(1/(2M_s)).</p>\n","answer":28.96,"tol":0.005,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l16-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Bode integral of ln|S| for a loop with one open-loop RHP pole at s = 1?</p>\n","explain":"<p>π times the sum of RHP poles.</p>\n","answer":3.1416,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l16-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Sensor noise reaches the output through…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The loop tracks the measurement.</p>\n","options":["the integral","S","T","the plant only"],"answer":2},{"id":"p13-l16-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The waterbed effect says…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The integral of ln|S| is fixed.</p>\n","options":["feedback removes noise","T and S are equal","S is always below 1","reducing |S| in one band raises it in another"],"answer":3}],"p13-l17":[{"id":"p13-l17-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase lag in degrees of a 2 s delay at 0.5 rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>ωθ = 1 rad.</p>\n","answer":57.3,"tol":0.002,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l17-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase margin in degrees of 0.5e^(−2s)/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Crossover at 0.5 rad/s.</p>\n","answer":32.7,"tol":0.01,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l17-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Dead time in s for 3 m at 0.5 m/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Distance over speed.</p>\n","answer":6,"tol":0,"unit":"s"},{"id":"p13-l17-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase error in degrees of the first-order Padé at ωθ = 0.5?</p>\n","explain":"<p>−2 arctan(ωθ/2) versus −ωθ.</p>\n","answer":0.58,"tol":0.03,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l17-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>With an exact model, the Smith predictor makes the closed loop…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The delay moves outside the loop.</p>\n","options":["identical to plain PI","unstable","the delay-free closed loop followed by the delay","delay-free"],"answer":2},{"id":"p13-l17-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The first-order Padé approximation has…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Its zero is at +2/θ.</p>\n","options":["a right-half-plane zero","a double pole","gain that falls with frequency","no phase"],"answer":0}],"p13-l18":[{"id":"p13-l18-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Gravity torque in N·m of 0.5 kg at 0.3 m, arm horizontal?</p>\n","explain":"<p>mgℓ.</p>\n","answer":1.4715,"tol":0.001,"unit":"N·m"},{"id":"p13-l18-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Static PD error in rad from that gravity at θ = 1 rad with K_p = 20?</p>\n","explain":"<p>mgℓ sin θ / K_p.</p>\n","answer":0.0619,"tol":0.01,"unit":"rad"},{"id":"p13-l18-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Inertial feedforward torque in N·m at peak reference acceleration 0.6 rad/s² with J = 0.05?</p>\n","explain":"<p>J θ̈_r.</p>\n","answer":0.03,"tol":0.001,"unit":"N·m"},{"id":"p13-l18-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Fraction of the error left if feedforward removes 90 % of the required torque (ideal linear case)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Feedback handles the remainder.</p>\n","answer":0.1,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l18-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Does adding feedforward change closed-loop stability?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The loop transfer function is unchanged.</p>\n","options":["only for integrators","no, it acts outside the loop","yes, it adds poles","it always destabilises"],"answer":1},{"id":"p13-l18-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Gravity compensation on a robot joint is an example of…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A known disturbance cancelled at the input.</p>\n","options":["a Smith predictor","derivative filtering","integral action","disturbance feedforward"],"answer":3}],"p13-l19":[{"id":"p13-l19-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Current-loop proportional gain in V/A for L = 2 mH and ω_i = 3000 rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p,i = L ω_i.</p>\n","answer":6,"tol":0.001,"unit":"V/A"},{"id":"p13-l19-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Current-loop integral gain in V/(A·s) for R = 1.2 Ω and ω_i = 3000 rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_i,i = R ω_i, which puts the zero at R/L.</p>\n","answer":3600,"tol":0.001,"unit":"V/(A·s)"},{"id":"p13-l19-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Speed-loop gain in A per rad/s for J = 2e-4, k = 0.05 and ω_s = 300 rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p,s = J ω_s / k.</p>\n","answer":1.2,"tol":0.001,"unit":"A/(rad/s)"},{"id":"p13-l19-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>With 10× separation per level below a current loop at ω_i = 3000 rad/s, what is the position bandwidth in rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Two levels of 10× separation.</p>\n","answer":30,"tol":0.001,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l19-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Which loop is innermost in a motor servo cascade?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The fastest dynamics go innermost.</p>\n","options":["position","temperature","current (torque)","speed"],"answer":2},{"id":"p13-l19-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why does the position loop usually need no integral term?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The speed PI holds zero speed error under constant load, and the plant from speed to position is already an integrator.</p>\n","options":["the current loop removes all errors","integrators are unstable","the speed loop’s integrator already rejects load torque","position cannot have steady-state error"],"answer":2}],"p13-l20":[{"id":"p13-l20-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Derivative filter coefficient T_f/(T_f + T_s) for T_f = 10 ms and T_s = 1 ms?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Backward Euler of the first-order filter.</p>\n","answer":0.90909,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l20-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Integrator increment per sample for K_i = 10, T_s = 1 ms and e = 0.5?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_i T_s e.</p>\n","answer":0.005,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l20-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase lost in degrees to a 50 µs latency at a 3000 rad/s crossover?</p>\n","explain":"<p>ω_c t_d in radians, converted.</p>\n","answer":8.594,"tol":0.01,"unit":"deg"},{"id":"p13-l20-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>CPU load in percent of a 50 µs ISR at 10 kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Execution time over period.</p>\n","answer":50,"tol":0.001,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p13-l20-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why take the derivative on the measurement rather than the error?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The setpoint is piecewise constant; differentiating it gives spikes.</p>\n","options":["it removes the need for a filter","a setpoint step then causes no derivative kick","it makes the loop faster","it is more accurate"],"answer":1},{"id":"p13-l20-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Conditional-integration anti-windup stops the integrator when…</p>\n","explain":"<p>It integrates normally as soon as the error would bring the output back.</p>\n","options":["the error is zero","the derivative is large","the output is saturated and the error pushes further into saturation","the sample period is late"],"answer":2}]}